        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T14:54:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about having `recordDraw` return `std::pair\u003cDrawParams*, Layer*\u003e`? That will be a nicer signature when we are just in the layer system and the sort key system can just ignore the return values",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "6f0032f8e6c5ec66269a7c7ae5d34a7f0614d1a8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e4e3c97_70a4b12d",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawListBase.h",
        "patchSetId": 48
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T16:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree it makes the signature simpler, but it makes calling the function awkward. Right now we rely on the outer pointer being non-null to signal what type of draw we have, i.e. when `captureParams` is not null, then it is depthOnly.\n\nTo do this with the new signature, we would have to create empty `DrawParams` and `Layers` so that we can pass in a non-null ptr, and then overwrite those. \n\nNow if there is a way to get around this? Is there such a thing as an empty but not null ptr? Alternatively we could just pass or template bools in lol.",
      "parentUuid": "d9578abc_295e3f96",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "6f0032f8e6c5ec66269a7c7ae5d34a7f0614d1a8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df274e06_dd099a95",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawListBase.h",
        "patchSetId": 48
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-12T18:19:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can use the `paintID` to determine if it\u0027s depth-only, it will be an InvalidID() for depth-only draws and valid for anything else.\n\nThen you can always return the `DrawParams*` result, and the outer context ignores it (drawGeometry) or saves it (ClipStack).\n\nThe only weird thing about this new signature is that we are passing in the stop layer and then updating the stop layer, so it\u0027d look like:\n\n```\nstd::tie(prevLayer, captureParam) \u003d list-\u003erecordDraw(...., prevLayer);\n```\n\nin the case we don\u0027t care about the DrawParams, you should be able to use `std::ignore` in the tie call.",
      "parentUuid": "7e4e3c97_70a4b12d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "6f0032f8e6c5ec66269a7c7ae5d34a7f0614d1a8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
